" :SongwriterTabChord (songwriter#tab#TabChord): insert a chord on a new line
" above the tab block, aligned to the cursor column.

Given (insert chord above tab block at cursor column):
  e|-----------4--|--1-----------|
  B|--------1-----|-----2-----2--|
  G|--3-----0--0--|-----1--0--0--|
  D|--------1-----|-----1--------|
  A|--4--3--------|--1-----1-----|
  E|--3-----------|--1-----------|

Execute (insert chord above tab block at cursor column):
  call cursor(1, 14)
  call songwriter#tab#TabChord('Am7')
Then:
  AssertEqual '             Am7', getline(1)
  AssertEqual 'e|-----------4--|--1-----------|', getline(2)
  AssertEqual 'B|--------1-----|-----2-----2--|', getline(3)

Given (insert chord at column 1 (start of tab)):
  e|--4--|--1--|
  B|------|-----|
  G|------|-----|
  D|------|-----|
  A|------|-----|
  E|------|-----|

Execute (insert chord at column 1 (start of tab)):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#tab#TabChord('C')
Then:
  AssertEqual 'C', getline(1)
  AssertEqual 'e|--4--|--1--|', getline(2)

Given (insert chord in middle of tab block):
  e|--4--|--1--|
  B|------|-----|
  G|------|-----|
  D|------|-----|
  A|------|-----|
  E|------|-----|

Execute (insert chord in middle of tab block):
  call cursor(3, 8)
  call songwriter#tab#TabChord('Dm')
Then:
  AssertEqual '       Dm', getline(1)
  AssertEqual 'e|--4--|--1--|', getline(2)

Given (no-op on non-tab lines):
  this is prose

Execute (no-op on non-tab lines):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#tab#TabChord('Am')
Expect:
  this is prose
